## Coordinates

By default ggplot uses Cartesian coordinates (x,y), but you can modify them easily using ```coord_XXXX()``` functions. 




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data = mpg, 
       mapping = aes(x =class, y=hwy)) +
  geom_boxplot()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-2-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="4"}
ggplot(data = mpg, 
       mapping = aes(x =class, y=hwy)) +
  geom_boxplot() +
  coord_flip()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-3-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::





## Maps

You can use maps for your plots, and with `coord_quickmap()` it will compute the accurate ratio for the maps.




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(maps)
nz <- map_data("nz")

ggplot(nz, aes(long, lat, group = group)) +
  geom_polygon(fill = "white", 
               colour = "black")
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-4-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="4"}
ggplot(nz, aes(long, lat, group = group)) +
  geom_polygon(fill = "white", 
               colour = "black") +
  coord_quickmap()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-5-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::





## Polar Plots

We can change how to represent some data, using another visualization style. Imagine we have the following plot...




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(diamonds) +
  geom_bar(
    aes(x = cut, fill=cut),
    show.legend = F,
    width = 1
  ) +
  theme(aspect.ratio = 1) +
  labs(x=NULL, y=NULL) +
  coord_flip()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::




We can change it to much more interesting style...




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code  code-line-numbers="9"}
ggplot(diamonds) +
  geom_bar(
    aes(x = cut, fill=cut),
    show.legend = F,
    width = 1
  ) +
  theme(aspect.ratio = 1) +
  labs(x=NULL, y=NULL) +
  coord_polar()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](04_05_customization_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::
